                            "attributes": "{\"attributeId\":\"1be88f86-bb11-429c-824c-25aa23948ffa\",\"fieldName\":\"customField1077\",\"name\":\"Hosting Solution\",\"nameKey\":\"AssetsCustomField1077\",\"attributeType\":\"none\",\"responseType\":\"single-select\",\"displayAnswerType\":\"button\",\"showQuestionDetailsLink\":false,\"requireJustification\":false,\"allowLaws\":true}",
                            "friendlyName": "Hosting Solution",
                            "description": "<p>Hosting is where and how the application runs (who owns/manages the infrastructure).&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><ul><li><strong>On-prem:</strong>&nbsp;Technology or software that runs on computers or servers located at your company’s physical site (your own data center or office - e.g., installed on your company's servers).</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><strong>Cloud:</strong>&nbsp;Technology or software that runs on servers managed by a third-party provider and accessed over the internet (e.g., AWS, Microsoft Azure, Google Cloud).</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><strong>Hybrid:</strong>&nbsp;A mix of on-prem and cloud solutions. Some parts run on your company’s servers, while others run in the cloud (e.g., vendor supplies POS terminals for restaurants (on-prem hardware) but manages reporting and analytics in the cloud via AWS).</li></ul><p><br></p>",
